      "slug": "why-auroras-have-different-colors",
      "title": "极光为什么有绿有红？天空其实在做一场“原子灯光秀”",
      "verification_status": "verified",
      "core_facts": [
        {"fact": "极光由高能粒子碰撞并激发高层大气原子和分子，退激时发光。", "status": "verified", "sources": ["NASA Auroras", "NOAA Aurora Tutorial"]},
        {"fact": "原子氧约557.7 nm发射产生常见绿色，约630.0 nm发射产生红色。", "status": "verified", "sources": ["NOAA Aurora Tutorial", "NASA Red and Green Aurora Australis"]},
        {"fact": "氧的红绿发射与氮的蓝/粉紫发射对应不同典型高度和碰撞条件。", "status": "verified", "sources": ["NASA Auroras", "NASA The Atmosphere After Dark", "NOAA Aurora Tutorial"]},
        {"fact": "数字相机可记录肉眼在暗处难以分辨的弱极光色彩。", "status": "verified", "sources": ["NOAA Aurora Tutorial"]}
      ],
